levels/
Level JSON API Map (Version 1.0 Freeze)

This folder contains every playable level.

The Match-3 engine never hardcodes a level. Every aspect of gameplay is loaded from a level JSON file.

Folder
levels/
    level001.json
    level002.json
    ...
    level050.json

Future versions can simply add:

level051.json
level052.json
...

without modifying the engine.

Common JSON Structure

Every level uses the same schema.

{
    "level_id": 1,
    "name": "",
    "description": "",
    "difficulty": "",
    "board": {},
    "moves": {},
    "objectives": [],
    "tile_pool": {},
    "powerups": {},
    "obstacles": {},
    "rewards": {},
    "tutorial": {},
    "story": {},
    "audio": {},
    "background": {},
    "settings": {},
    "metadata": {}
}
level_id

Unique level number.

"level_id": 1
name

Display name.

"name": "Level 1"
description

Optional.

"description": "Learn the basics."
difficulty

Possible values

TUTORIAL
EASY
MEDIUM
HARD
BOSS

Example

"difficulty": "TUTORIAL"
board

Defines the game board.

{
    "rows": 8,
    "columns": 8,
    "tile_size": 96,
    "spawn_points": [],
    "blocked_cells": [],
    "locked_cells": []
}
rows
"rows": 8
columns
"columns": 8
tile_size
"tile_size": 96
